menu "airflash"
    config UPD_WIFI_SSID
        string "Wi-Fi SSID (2.4 GHz)"

    config UPD_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "Wi-Fi password"

    config UPD_HOSTNAME
        string "mDNS hostname (<name>.local), empty = airflash-XXXX"
        default ""
        help
            Empty: airflash-XXXX, XXXX = the last 4 hex digits of the Wi-Fi MAC (e.g. airflash-9220),
            so several boards on one network don't all claim the same name. The updater and the
            airflash component use the same rule, so a board keeps one name in the app and the updater.
            Also sent as the DHCP hostname (router's client list) where airflash brings up Wi-Fi itself.

    config UPD_TOKEN
        string "Pairing token (empty = generate one)"
        default ""
        help
            Empty: the build creates a random token once per laptop (~/.airflash/token) and uses it for
            every board installed from this laptop.
            Set: use this token instead (printable ASCII without spaces, 1-63 characters), e.g. one shared
            by a team. If ~/.airflash/token doesn't exist yet, the build saves it there for the airflash tool.
            Stored only in this sdkconfig and in the board's upd_cfg partition, never compiled into the
            firmware. A random token is stronger than a short custom one.
endmenu
